{"tool_name":"longislnd","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"longislnd","home":"https://github.com/bioinform/longislnd","license":"CC-BY-NC-SA-4.0","summary":"LongISLND is a software package designed to simulate sequencing data according to the characteristics of third generation, single-molecule sequencing technologies.","addition_date":"2018-11-27T07:54:18Z","last_update_date":"2019-01-13T17:33:05Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:longislnd","credit":[{"email":"bina.rd@roche.com","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]},{"name":"Bayo Lau","orcidid":"http://orcid.org/0000-0001-7243-9221","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Contributor"]}],"documentation":[{"type":["User manual"],"url":"http://bioinform.github.io/longislnd/"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Sequence assembly","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0310"}]}],"name":"LongISLND","operating_system":["Linux"],"owner":"daniel_stefan","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/bioinformatics/btw602","metadata":{"abstract":"\u00a9 The Author 2016. Published by Oxford University Press.LongISLND is a software package designed to simulate sequencing data according to the characteristics of third generation, single-molecule sequencing technologies. The general software architecture is easily extendable, as demonstrated by the emulation of Pacific Biosciences (PacBio) multi-pass sequencing with P5 and P6 chemistries, producing data in FASTQ, H5, and the latest PacBio BAM format. We demonstrate its utility by downstream processing with consensus building and variant calling.","authors":[{"name":"Asadi N.B."},{"name":"Dallett C."},{"name":"Fang L.T."},{"name":"Lam H.Y.K."},{"name":"Lau B."},{"name":"Mohiyuddin M."},{"name":"Mu J.C."}],"citationCount":10,"date":"2016-12-15T00:00:00Z","journal":"Bioinformatics","title":"LongiSLND: In silico sequencing of lengthy and noisy datatypes"},"pmcid":"PMC51670